# 12. Git Stash

```bash
git stash
git stash list
git stash pop stash@{0}
git stash apply stash@{0}
git stash push -m "description"
```

I tried switching branches with uncommitted changes and Git stopped me:

```text
error: Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by checkout
```

I then used:

```bash
git stash
```

to temporarily save my work.

## Pop vs Apply

| Command           | Action                                       |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `git stash pop`   | Applies stash and removes it if successful   |
| `git stash apply` | Applies stash but keeps it in the stash list |

### Practice Mistake

Wrong:

```bash
git pop a705ad5
```

Correct:

```bash
git stash pop stash@{0}
```

> A commit hash is not the same as a stash reference.

